WEBVTT

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:03.570
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:09.090
I want to begin rebuilding 
the real Cyberse World.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.320
Rebuild Cyberse World...

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:17.300
To do that, we'll create a new base 
and put humans under our control.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.530
Isn't there any way to coexist with humans?

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.670
It seems you've become attached to humans.

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:26.610
The Light Ignis...

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:29.340
You made it, Playmaker.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:40.720
Since you heard our discussion, 
we can't let you go.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:49.800
I've returned to the stage of destiny!

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:54.720
In the name of the Knights 
of Hanoi, I will kill you!

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:17.340
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:24.130
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:31.450
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:38.030
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:44.770
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:52.000
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:58.710
I want to share your pain

00:02:34.090 --> 00:02:35.030
Revolver!

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:37.230
What?  What's going on?

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:41.410
I told you I wouldn't run from my fate.

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:43.510
That I would return.

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.440
Revolver.  Dr. Kogami's son.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:49.710
Run, Revolver!

00:02:57.130 --> 00:03:02.090
Oh yeah.  You can use our algorithm.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:08.330
I'm not foolish enough to enter 
the enemy's HQ without a plan.

00:03:08.540 --> 00:03:10.840
Is he referring to us?

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.570
Yes.

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:14.930
I'm surprised you found this place.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:18.580
We're always monitoring the network.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.180
Don't underestimate me, Ignis.

00:03:20.470 --> 00:03:23.780
I had Echo watching guard.

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:28.140
I have those who act as my shield and sword.

00:03:28.140 --> 00:03:30.520
And very intelligent.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:32.970
Spectre and the three Knights of Hanoi!

00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:36.040
They're all together?

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:42.470
Motor Worm Spreader Queen 
attacks you directly!

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:50.180
Appear, Link 3 Dark Mummy Surgical Forceps!

00:03:53.080 --> 00:03:58.820
Necro Darwin, end this 
DNA-less lower life form!

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:06.420
Come out!  Link 3 Sunavalon Dryanome!

00:04:08.220 --> 00:04:12.930
Even if you attack as a group, 
you're no match for us.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:15.930
I'm continuing my father's will.

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:19.170
I must finish the work he left undone.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:22.940
But we're the ones continuing 
Dr. Kogami's will.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:25.140
As humanity's successor.

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:30.520
Silence!  I'll crush those arrogant thoughts!

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:35.500
Since you Ignis have started 
teaming up, I can no longer delay.

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.760
I'll annihilate you!  Get ready!

00:04:38.980 --> 00:04:42.490
Annihilate?  How extreme.

00:04:42.760 --> 00:04:44.430
Wait, Revolver!

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:47.740
If you fight them now, 
there's no turning back!

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:51.100
I never planned on turning back.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:56.050
Your father Dr. Kogami said 
humans were the problem!

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:04.080
If humans view AI as the enemy, 
AI will view humans as the enemy.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:07.050
If you're hostile, the more 
hostility you get in return!

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:12.890
That's why you're searching for a 
way to coexist with no hostility?

00:05:12.890 --> 00:05:16.100
That's right.  There must be a way.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:19.480
Just like how you created a way for me!

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:23.970
I told you I strongly regretted doing that.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:31.180
And I also regret that my 
father created the Ignis.

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:34.940
Playmaker, you spoke of a way to coexist.

00:05:34.940 --> 00:05:39.680
Then why are they stopping 
you from finding it?

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:43.360
Umm, you see, this is a misunderstanding.

00:05:43.360 --> 00:05:46.900
You underestimate the Ignis.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:49.890
Your behavior disgusts me!

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:55.000
Hatred and revenge prevents 
you from truly moving forward!

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:57.370
I know that more than anyone!

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:03.340
What moves me forward are the 
ideas that my dead father left me.

00:06:04.120 --> 00:06:06.810
Which is the annihilation of the Ignis!

00:06:07.020 --> 00:06:09.810
He's not wavering at all.  Bravo.

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:14.520
Talking to him is pointless.

00:06:14.530 --> 00:06:18.490
Because right or wrong, he wants to erase us.

00:06:18.720 --> 00:06:20.230
Seems so.

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:26.760
Let's teach him that all 
his effort is worthless.

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:28.100
I'll do it.

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:31.070
Fine, Wind Ignis.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:33.540
I'll erase you first!

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.780
Hey, wait a sec!

00:06:35.780 --> 00:06:39.440
If you're here to rescue 
us, let us out first?

00:06:39.440 --> 00:06:42.880
You have the wrong idea.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.990
Don't forget that you're also an Ignis.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.660
An enemy that must be destroyed!

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:50.740
Wait a sec!

00:06:50.740 --> 00:06:55.330
I've been teaming up with 
Playmaker to save LINK VRAINS!

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:58.700
No one asked you to do that.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.170
You are correct.

00:07:01.560 --> 00:07:07.170
Playmaker, that Ignis has 
dulled your decision making.

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:12.610
I'll say this once - The Ignis 
are a threat to humanity.

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:14.580
No more delays.

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:19.040
Revolver, don't let Dr. 
Kogami's ideas tie you down!

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.050
See with your own eyes!  
Think with your own thoughts!

00:07:22.260 --> 00:07:26.020
If you're imprisoned by your 
past, you have no future!

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:32.260
Playmaker's saying this?  You wanted 
revenge and was tied down by your past.

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:35.270
I'm no longer tied down by my past!

00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:40.870
Then witness with your own eyes 
the truth about the Ignis.

00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:49.100
But if you stand in my 
way, I'll bury you too.

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:53.090
This definitely can't be stopped anymore!

00:07:54.690 --> 00:07:58.720
I finished analyzing the 
location where Yusaku entered.

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:01.460
He doesn't seem like he's coming back.

00:08:01.460 --> 00:08:03.700
Something must have happened.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:05.900
That's not necessarily true.

00:08:06.290 --> 00:08:11.140
He doesn't trust Windy, but I want to.

00:08:11.140 --> 00:08:12.500
Cuz he's an ally.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:17.210
But since he hasn't returned, 
there may be trouble.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:20.050
Takeru, can you go?

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:26.580
I created data that'll temporarily 
cut the Ignis's program.

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:29.450
It might come in handy, just in case.

00:08:29.820 --> 00:08:31.650
Your Duel Disk.

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:39.640
But I don't know how effective it'll be.

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:44.650
This program will also send me your video.

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:45.870
Understood.

00:08:46.100 --> 00:08:47.900
I'm counting on you, Takeru.

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:49.610
Be careful.

00:08:56.690 --> 00:09:00.120
Deck set!  Into the VRAINS!

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:30.140
What's this?

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:36.420
What happened?

00:09:37.190 --> 00:09:40.000
Playmaker!  Ai!

00:09:40.730 --> 00:09:43.230
Something bad happened.

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:46.000
Let's search for Playmaker.

00:09:51.160 --> 00:09:54.280
It's starting!  It's really starting!

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.410
What should we do, Playmaker?

00:09:56.700 --> 00:09:59.880
There's nothing we can do in our situation.

00:10:00.360 --> 00:10:05.880
Since you pummeled Playmaker, I've been 
curious to test your skills at least once.

00:10:06.220 --> 00:10:10.190
Fine.  But there won't be a second time!

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:15.870
Duel!

00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:21.270
Please go first.  I'll see what you do.

00:10:21.270 --> 00:10:24.020
That overconfidence will cost your life.

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:25.510
My turn!

00:10:25.510 --> 00:10:29.510
I activate the Field Spell, 
Boot Sector Launch!

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:33.980
I Special Summon up to 
two Rokkets from my hand.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:39.590
I Special Summon Anesthrokket 
Dragon and Magnarokket Dragon!

00:10:40.940 --> 00:10:47.190
Due to Boot Sector Launch's effect, 
Rokkets gain 300 ATK and DEF.

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:51.530
Is Revolver already gonna do it?

00:10:51.930 --> 00:10:55.670
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:10:56.410 --> 00:11:01.170
The summoning conditions 
are two Dark Dragons!

00:11:03.110 --> 00:11:04.410
Link Summon!

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:09.380
Appear, Link 2 Dillingerous Dragon!

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:15.550
Seems you want to defeat 
me as fast as possible.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:19.530
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:23.030
You act like you're prepared for anything.

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:27.270
But I feel like human intellect is shallow.

00:11:27.270 --> 00:11:31.150
Then test whether it's shallow or not.

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:33.000
I will.

00:11:33.280 --> 00:11:35.780
My turn!  I draw!

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:43.740
When there's a monster on your field, I can 
Special Summon Stormrider Griffore from my hand!

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:46.450
As expected, a Cyberse card.

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:50.770
And when there's a card in 
your Spell & Trap Zone...

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:55.880
...I can Special Summon Stormrider 
Hippogriff from my hand!

00:11:56.160 --> 00:11:59.860
Appear!  My raging circuit!

00:12:00.830 --> 00:12:05.240
I set Griffore and Hippogriff 
in the Link Markers!

00:12:06.800 --> 00:12:08.010
Link Summon!

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:13.150
Appear, Link 2 Stormridership Rockbuster!

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:21.090
It has more ATK than Dillingerous Dragon!

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:25.490
I activate the Field Spell, 
Stormrider Turbulence!

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:31.460
Due to its effect, Stormriders 
on the field gain 300 ATK!

00:12:33.430 --> 00:12:37.170
Then I summon Stormrider Harpiarm!

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:46.520
Due to Stormrider Turbulence's 
effect, Harpiarm gains 300 ATK!

00:12:46.740 --> 00:12:49.750
Then Rockbuster's effect activates!

00:12:50.420 --> 00:12:53.540
When there are no cards 
in my Spell & Trap Zone...

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:58.560
...and a monster is summoned or Special 
Summoned next to this card's link...

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:02.530
...two cards in your Spell 
& Trap Zone are destroyed!

00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:03.760
What?

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:06.730
Those two set cards are gone.

00:13:10.470 --> 00:13:15.350
Whoa!  One of the set 
cards was Magic Cylinder.

00:13:15.350 --> 00:13:16.440
That was close.

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:18.670
Magic Cylinder.

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:22.660
During battle, that trap 
card negates the opponent's

00:13:22.660 --> 00:13:27.190
monster's attack and deals 
damage equal to its ATK.

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:30.330
Seriously?  He already has Mirror Force!

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:33.660
He uses incredible cards!

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:39.130
Revolver always surpasses our expectations.

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:46.600
When Rockbuster uses its effect, I can't 
activate or set spell and trap cards that turn.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:54.460
His strategy is to destroy his set cards 
to break his defense, and then battle.

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:57.250
It's a strong first punch!

00:13:58.200 --> 00:14:00.580
Windy is quite skilled.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:05.090
But Revolver will definitely 
do something too.

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:12.330
I don't like either of them, but 
which winner will allow me to leave?

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:15.710
The odds are low, regardless of the winner.

00:14:15.710 --> 00:14:17.070
No way!

00:14:17.340 --> 00:14:22.210
From my graveyard, I activate the trap 
card, Reverse Engineering's effect.

00:14:22.210 --> 00:14:23.040
What?

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:25.820
By banishing this card from the graveyard...

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:31.800
...I can set a trap card from the 
graveyard that was destroyed this turn.

00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:36.490
The card set by this effect can 
be activated that same turn.

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:41.240
I set Magic Cylinder from my graveyard!

00:14:43.560 --> 00:14:45.800
Welcome back, Magic Cylinder!

00:14:45.800 --> 00:14:51.370
He set that card knowing that his spell 
and trap cards would be destroyed.

00:14:51.370 --> 00:14:55.870
Wow!  He countered while facing a battle!

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:59.240
Winning or losing the duel 
isn't what's important.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:02.230
What will happen as a result is.

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:04.380
Huh?  What do you mean?

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:07.890
If Revolver wins, the Ignis 
will be killed quicker.

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:14.090
If Windy wins, the Ignis will 
decide to conquer humans quicker.

00:15:14.090 --> 00:15:18.560
No!  Either way, it'll be tough for me!

00:15:18.780 --> 00:15:22.380
What's wrong?  You're not going to battle?

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:26.670
Even a fool wouldn't battle when 
he knows he'll take damage.

00:15:26.880 --> 00:15:29.670
But it won't go as you hope.

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:33.280
You will choose your own form of pain!

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:34.750
There's no escape!

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:35.980
What?

00:15:35.980 --> 00:15:43.020
When you end your turn, Dillingerous Dragon 
destroys a monster that didn't attack...

00:15:43.020 --> 00:15:46.760
...and you take damage equal to its ATK!

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:49.060
That card's crazy.

00:15:49.430 --> 00:15:54.790
Umm...  If he battles, Magic 
Cylinder will intercept it.

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:59.830
If he doesn't battle, Dillingerous 
Dragon's effect awaits.

00:15:59.830 --> 00:16:01.310
That means...

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:04.310
He is induced to attack.

00:16:04.310 --> 00:16:06.540
What an interesting strategy.

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:08.000
Now choose.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:11.520
Self-destruction without battling?  
Or pain from battling?

00:16:13.100 --> 00:16:15.290
Then of course, I choose to battle.

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:18.490
Rockbuster attacks Dillingerous Dragon!

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:23.460
I activate the trap card, Magic Cylinder!

00:16:23.680 --> 00:16:30.940
When you attack, that monster's attack is 
negated, and you take damage equal to its ATK!

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:33.300
2300 damage!

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:38.680
I don't like pain, so I 
activate Harpiarm's effect!

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:45.650
When you activate a trap, I switch this card 
to defense position to negate and destroy it!

00:16:48.600 --> 00:16:51.620
Now there are no more 
obstacles in this battle.

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:03.130
This is the pain from battling.

00:17:03.500 --> 00:17:04.970
I end my turn.

00:17:05.180 --> 00:17:10.710
Windy was supposed to take damage, 
but Revolver took damage instead.

00:17:11.000 --> 00:17:15.080
Things hardly go as you imagine.

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:20.180
I bet Dr. Kogami also thought 
the same thing about us Ignis.

00:17:20.180 --> 00:17:24.790
Even if we stumble, our conviction 
will lead us on the right path.

00:17:24.790 --> 00:17:27.720
That's what I learned from my father.

00:17:28.230 --> 00:17:30.660
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:31.060 --> 00:17:33.540
Boot Sector Launch's effect activates.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:37.370
I Special Summon Rokkets from my 
graveyard in defense position!

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:39.700
Come!  Anesthrokket!

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:42.340
And Magnarokket Dragon!

00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:49.050
When a Rokket is Special Summoned, I Special 
Summon Dillingerous Dragon from the graveyard.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:51.780
Resurrect, Dillingerous Dragon!

00:17:56.210 --> 00:18:02.330
Since this effect Special Summoned 
Dillingerous Dragon, it's banished if it leaves the field.

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.800
Lots came out of the graveyard.

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:09.270
Appear!  The future circuit 
that lights up my path!

00:18:09.540 --> 00:18:12.740
The summoning conditions are 
at least three Effect Monsters!

00:18:13.140 --> 00:18:21.180
I set Anesthrokket, Magnarokket and Link 
2 Dillingerous Dragon in the Link Markers!

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:25.360
Link Summon!

00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:30.290
Appear, Link 4 Borreload Dragon!

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:39.860
I'll end you with this battle!

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:43.830
Borreload Dragon is your ace monster.

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:47.470
But that monster is Link 
4, just as I planned.

00:18:47.470 --> 00:18:48.620
What?

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:52.340
Learn that things don't go as planned.

00:18:53.060 --> 00:18:55.340
Rockbuster's effect activates!

00:18:55.560 --> 00:19:00.140
When a Link 3 or higher monster 
is Link Summoned to your field...

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:04.420
... I set one trap card from 
your graveyard on my field.

00:19:04.420 --> 00:19:08.330
And the set card can be activated that turn.

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:12.460
A trap card in the graveyard?  
Then it must be...

00:19:12.460 --> 00:19:16.230
I set Magic Cylinder from your graveyard!

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:23.220
If I remember correctly, Magic Cylinder 
negates your monster's attack...

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:27.980
...and you take damage equal to its ATK.

00:19:29.740 --> 00:19:32.350
It's the opposite of last turn!

00:19:32.560 --> 00:19:33.820
It won't work.

00:19:35.380 --> 00:19:42.830
Borreload Dragon lowers the ATK and 
DEF of a faceup monster by 500.

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:44.060
Lowers?

00:19:44.060 --> 00:19:49.300
And you can't activate any effects 
against this effect's activation.

00:19:49.700 --> 00:19:51.540
An anti-enemy Rokket!

00:19:52.060 --> 00:20:00.510
By using this effect when Borreload Dragon 
attacks, Magic Cylinder can't activate its effect.

00:20:00.510 --> 00:20:03.200
You thought you executed a surprise attack.

00:20:03.200 --> 00:20:06.980
But you should learn that 
things don't go as planned.

00:20:06.990 --> 00:20:09.220
So wanna try to attack?

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:14.690
Of course.  I'll defeat you 
and destroy that other Ignis!

00:20:18.920 --> 00:20:22.390
There's no point thinking about later.

00:20:22.390 --> 00:20:25.330
Because you're the one who'll be destroyed.

00:20:25.620 --> 00:20:28.170
Stormrider Turbulence's effect!

00:20:28.780 --> 00:20:34.140
When you Special Summon a Link Monster with 
equal or more Link Markers than Rockbuster...

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:38.480
...that monster's effects are 
negated until your next turn!

00:20:40.080 --> 00:20:44.080
Stormrider Turbulence's additional effect!

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:50.630
When a Stormrider is in the Extra Monster 
Zone, you must attack that Stormrider!

00:20:50.980 --> 00:20:54.370
Rockbuster is in the Extra Monster Zone!

00:20:54.580 --> 00:21:01.710
Borreload has higher ATK, but Windy 
has Magic Cylinder set on his field.

00:21:01.940 --> 00:21:05.490
You will take 3000 damage.

00:21:05.700 --> 00:21:07.950
Now hurt yourself!

00:21:08.320 --> 00:21:09.600
Battle.

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:13.480
Borreload Dragon attacks Rockbuster!

00:21:19.620 --> 00:21:22.840
I activate the trap card, Magic Cylinder!

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:25.860
Hurt yourself with your own trap card!

00:21:39.630 --> 00:21:42.180
His LP are instantly down to 300!

00:21:44.380 --> 00:21:47.480
You talked about annihilating us.

00:21:47.480 --> 00:21:52.170
But you'll fail to even defeat me.

00:21:52.170 --> 00:21:55.290
Your calculations are sloppy for an AI.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:22:01.900
I'll teach the correct answer 
to this defective AI!

00:22:19.300 --> 00:22:25.640
Memories that don't disappear
And memories that disappeared

00:22:25.870 --> 00:22:32.340
I quietly "NOW LOADING..." those scenes

00:22:32.770 --> 00:22:35.840
Memories left behind  Erased memories

00:22:35.840 --> 00:22:38.980
What was the PASSWORD again?

00:22:39.410 --> 00:22:43.580
ACCESS records  Restored memories

00:22:43.850 --> 00:22:46.550
Challenge "the you inside you"

00:22:51.260 --> 00:22:57.430
You're a Network  The 
World that spreads beyond

00:22:57.570 --> 00:23:00.570
With repeating "nows"

00:23:00.900 --> 00:23:04.510
What about you?  "Live for now"

00:23:04.670 --> 00:23:10.460
Grab the Shooting Star in 
the sky with both your hands

00:23:10.610 --> 00:23:13.750
Overcome "now" with all your might  Yell!

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:41.980
Even if he takes big damage, he has 
a chance as long as he still has LP.

00:23:42.200 --> 00:23:45.850
Revolver is full of confidence.

00:23:45.850 --> 00:23:49.960
He's not a fool who enters the 
enemy's HQ without a plan.

00:23:49.960 --> 00:23:54.780
He evolved and returned!  It's 
time to witness his power!

00:23:54.780 --> 00:23:57.710
That monster is...  It can't be!

